WEBVTT

00:01:44.090 --> 00:01:45.200
Win it, Ao!

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:46.240
Knock him out, Ao!

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:49.710
Joe! What’s wrong with you!? Get him! Get him!

00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:51.340
He’s drained his strength.

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:53.790
This fight has become entirely one-sided now, wouldn't you say, Yohko?

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:18.290
That’s the end of the round.

00:02:18.290 --> 00:02:19.200
Return to your corners.

00:02:23.530 --> 00:02:26.210
Joe! Pull yourself together! Joe!

00:02:39.590 --> 00:02:41.820
Joe, what’s happened to your basic technique?

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:44.600
Have you forgotten about your famous quick left jab?

00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:46.910
Cut it out, Nishi.

00:02:46.910 --> 00:02:48.850
You askin’ me to use the moves that old man taught me?

00:02:49.760 --> 00:02:52.950
Save that confidence for when you’re not in such bad shape.

00:02:52.950 --> 00:02:53.980
Listen, Joe,

00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:56.730
if you take more nasty hits in the next round, you’ll be out for sure.

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:59.330
Aoyama is already trying to win by KO.

00:02:59.330 --> 00:03:01.110
Those are the kind of punches he’s throwing at you!

00:03:03.710 --> 00:03:05.760
Ya stupid bastard, what the hell do ya think you’re doing!?

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:06.850
Shut your mouth!

00:03:06.850 --> 00:03:08.510
You got a problem with him?

00:03:08.510 --> 00:03:10.500
Uh, no, not really…

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:11.290
Joe!

00:03:12.590 --> 00:03:15.480
Aoyama thinks he can knock me out, eh?

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:19.290
Now that’cha mention it, he <i>was</i> aiming for my jaw a lot the second half of that round…

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:25.400
“The basics,” eh… ?

00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:31.160
Joe! The basics!

00:03:31.160 --> 00:03:32.310
You mustn’t forget the basics!

00:03:34.090 --> 00:03:35.610
I get it, Nishi.

00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:37.720
I guess that’s all I have to fall back on now.

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:42.110
For the Sake of Tomorrow #1: Left Jab.

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:43.860
To get your attack through,

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:48.110
or to slow down your opponent, you continuously punch with your left.

00:03:48.110 --> 00:03:51.120
Keep your left elbow close to your body, aim slightly inside,

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:53.440
and punch with a drilling motion.

00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:57.870
Then you strike!

00:03:58.860 --> 00:04:01.030
Using a straight right that tags onto the jabs…

00:04:01.030 --> 00:04:02.630
that power can be multiplied three or four fold!

00:04:09.350 --> 00:04:11.440
Asshole!

00:04:29.030 --> 00:04:30.640
Joe! Have you forgotten already?

00:04:30.640 --> 00:04:33.190
The basics! Get back to the basics!

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:44.290
Joe!

00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:49.510
Joe! The basics! The basics!

00:04:51.990 --> 00:04:53.650
It could have been a close fight.

00:05:07.620 --> 00:05:11.510
Joe! Joe! Joe! Joe! Joe!

00:05:15.070 --> 00:05:16.850
Where did those punches go?

00:05:16.850 --> 00:05:18.810
The punches you use to protect your freedom! {might be talking about episode 13 where Joe pretty much knocked every prisoner and guard in juvie in order not to be put into solitary}

00:05:18.810 --> 00:05:20.080
Where did it go!?

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:23.680
Those punches that compete with Rikiishi's, where did they go!?

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:31.070
Cut it out, Nishi.

00:05:31.070 --> 00:05:32.770
I’m trying my best.

00:05:32.770 --> 00:05:34.850
I’m fighting the fight of my life.

00:05:34.850 --> 00:05:37.050
I’m taking this fight seriously.

00:05:37.050 --> 00:05:38.450
But it’s not good enough.

00:05:38.450 --> 00:05:39.590
Not today…

00:05:39.590 --> 00:05:43.070
The punch that’s kept me going for this long doesn't work anymore.

00:05:43.070 --> 00:05:46.080
“Free,” my ass. “Boxing,” my ass.

00:05:57.950 --> 00:05:59.540
1!

00:05:59.540 --> 00:06:00.660
2!

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:01.540
3!

00:06:07.150 --> 00:06:09.140
I can hear the sound of the ocean.

00:06:09.140 --> 00:06:10.820
This feels great.

00:06:21.250 --> 00:06:22.660
Hey there, old man.

00:06:22.660 --> 00:06:24.280
Long time, no see.

00:06:24.280 --> 00:06:26.770
Where’ve you been all this time?

00:06:27.160 --> 00:06:28.770
Come on, let’s go home.

00:06:28.770 --> 00:06:31.340
Let’s stop doing these stupid and pointless things.

00:06:36.500 --> 00:06:37.890
Look at that, old man.

00:06:37.890 --> 00:06:38.870
It’s the ocean.

00:06:47.880 --> 00:06:49.250
Old man, cut it out.

00:06:49.250 --> 00:06:51.250
I've quit this stupid boxing.

00:06:54.890 --> 00:06:56.610
Old man, wait for me.

00:06:56.610 --> 00:06:58.390
I’m telling you, <i>I quit </i>!

00:07:21.700 --> 00:07:22.970
Don’t go, old man!

00:07:22.970 --> 00:07:25.990
I’ll do it! I’ll fight Aoyama!

00:07:25.990 --> 00:07:27.750
The real fight begins now!

00:07:32.480 --> 00:07:33.480
5!

00:07:33.480 --> 00:07:35.340
6!

00:07:35.340 --> 00:07:36.390
7!

00:07:37.600 --> 00:07:38.180
8!

00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:40.190
9!

00:07:43.480 --> 00:07:44.930
He stood up!

00:07:44.930 --> 00:07:46.060
Joe stood up!

00:07:46.060 --> 00:07:47.390
Joe!

00:07:47.390 --> 00:07:48.290
Look at that!

00:07:51.370 --> 00:07:52.870
He’s still gonna fight?

00:08:08.130 --> 00:08:09.310
Grandfather, look!

00:08:09.310 --> 00:08:11.130
Look at his eyes!

00:08:18.630 --> 00:08:20.470
Now that’s surprising.

00:08:20.470 --> 00:08:23.640
Completely unlike before, his eyes are very vulnerable now.

00:08:23.640 --> 00:08:25.470
This is the first time...

00:08:25.470 --> 00:08:27.450
The first time I've ever seen that look in his eyes.

00:08:35.780 --> 00:08:36.940
Fight!

00:08:40.790 --> 00:08:41.640
All right!

00:08:41.640 --> 00:08:44.420
Go all the way, Aoyama!

00:08:44.420 --> 00:08:45.790
Aoyama, don’t let us down!

00:09:48.810 --> 00:09:51.310
Hey, Yabuki! What’s wrong with you?

00:09:51.310 --> 00:09:53.360
Yeah, Yabuki, what’s that pose supposed to mean?

00:09:53.360 --> 00:09:55.880
Too many blows to the head make you lose your marbles?

00:09:55.880 --> 00:09:58.320
That stance is completely wrong for a boxer!

00:09:58.320 --> 00:10:00.990
You look like a turtle hiding in his shell!

00:10:00.990 --> 00:10:02.870
What a loser!

00:10:03.570 --> 00:10:05.440
You had enough and ready to give up?

00:10:05.440 --> 00:10:08.210
Why don’t you do us all a favor and give up already!

00:10:08.210 --> 00:10:10.460
I’ll bet you’re pretty sorry about being wrong, huh, Joe?

00:10:14.630 --> 00:10:17.350
They’re right… That’s a very undignified stance.

00:10:17.350 --> 00:10:19.560
It’s a very silly pose.

00:10:19.560 --> 00:10:21.030
Protecting his face…

00:10:21.030 --> 00:10:22.180
and protecting his chest.

00:10:22.180 --> 00:10:25.100
That pose is exactly like a turtle hiding in his shell.

00:10:25.100 --> 00:10:27.550
But… look at his vulnerability.

00:10:27.550 --> 00:10:29.520
Look at his sense of urgency!

00:10:29.520 --> 00:10:32.500
It’s a side of Joe no one has ever seen before!

00:10:32.500 --> 00:10:34.070
It’s a new Joe!

00:10:34.830 --> 00:10:36.250
Hey, old man.

00:10:36.250 --> 00:10:37.500
Hey, Aoyama.

00:10:37.500 --> 00:10:39.360
Don’t get me wrong...

00:10:39.360 --> 00:10:42.370
It’s not that I don’t fear you both as a team.

00:10:42.370 --> 00:10:44.400
To the awesomeness of fighting itself…

00:10:44.400 --> 00:10:45.810
to the deepness itself…

00:10:45.810 --> 00:10:47.990
to the bottomless strength and potential...

00:10:47.990 --> 00:10:49.080
I am bowing my head to that.

00:10:49.920 --> 00:10:50.920
Up until now…

00:10:50.920 --> 00:10:54.730
I thought Ao’s weak punches were harmless. I laughed at them.

00:10:54.730 --> 00:10:57.180
But from this point onward, I will fight much more defensively

00:10:57.180 --> 00:10:59.010
so that I won’t lose.

00:10:59.010 --> 00:11:00.060
But more than that...

00:11:00.060 --> 00:11:03.490
So that I can be victorious in this scary world of boxing.

00:11:03.490 --> 00:11:04.280
That’s it.

00:11:04.280 --> 00:11:05.320
Do you understand?

00:11:08.500 --> 00:11:09.800
Aren’t ya gonna fight?

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:16.590
You two, what’re ya just standing around for!?

00:11:16.590 --> 00:11:17.860
Just do it!

00:11:17.860 --> 00:11:18.650
Ao!

00:11:18.650 --> 00:11:20.770
Go get him!

00:11:20.770 --> 00:11:21.800
Ao!

00:11:30.330 --> 00:11:33.380
Aoyama-kun, go to him. Fight him.

00:11:33.380 --> 00:11:34.280
Y-Yes, Sir.

00:11:34.280 --> 00:11:35.330
But…

00:11:35.330 --> 00:11:38.340
Th-This is the first time I’ve seen that sort of “turtle” stance before.

00:11:38.690 --> 00:11:39.560
What’s wrong, Aoyama?

00:11:39.560 --> 00:11:40.920
Stop farting around!

00:11:40.920 --> 00:11:43.070
You’re just another punch away from a KO!

00:11:43.070 --> 00:11:43.820
Go, Ao!

00:11:43.820 --> 00:11:44.880
Now, I wonder about that assessment.

00:11:44.880 --> 00:11:48.040
With that stance, I think Joe has just become a more frightening adversary.

00:11:57.450 --> 00:12:00.320
Aoyama-kun, don’t let yourself get flustered just because your opponent’s stance has changed.

00:12:01.170 --> 00:12:03.320
He finally remembered to defend himself, that’s all.

00:12:03.760 --> 00:12:05.820
Come on. Go and fight him!

00:12:37.550 --> 00:12:38.650
Look what Joe is doing!

00:12:39.820 --> 00:12:42.610
His footwork… H-He’s started using his feet!

00:12:43.250 --> 00:12:44.490
Yohko, my dear.

00:12:44.490 --> 00:12:47.360
You chose a very good day for me to come here.

00:12:47.360 --> 00:12:48.620
I’m very grateful.

00:12:58.670 --> 00:12:59.960
What?

00:13:18.350 --> 00:13:20.860
That bastard, Joe. First footwork, now defense…{tlc reply: weeeeell, it was backwards in the same place in the manga but for some reason they switched it here.}

00:13:21.560 --> 00:13:25.030
He’s found the way I’ve been training Aoyama-kun, and is mirroring it back at him!

00:13:25.030 --> 00:13:30.720
To imitate the techniques of your opponent, and use them as a weapon against him…

00:13:30.720 --> 00:13:34.150
Unreal… I knew it! Joe’s abilities are phenomenal!

00:13:58.080 --> 00:13:59.650
H-He hit him!

00:13:59.650 --> 00:14:02.150
All right! Joe finally got a punch in!

00:14:02.510 --> 00:14:04.150
Return to your corners!

00:14:05.770 --> 00:14:07.310
Wonderful.

00:14:07.310 --> 00:14:10.110
What a wonderful match.

00:14:13.770 --> 00:14:15.630
Fight!

00:14:15.630 --> 00:14:20.940
Up until just now, I doubted that other boy, believing that Aoyama-kun would win.

00:14:20.940 --> 00:14:24.870
But, I'm not angry that I was wrong, I’m deeply moved.

00:14:24.870 --> 00:14:27.750
Boxing is a very wild sport by its nature.

00:14:27.750 --> 00:14:30.830
But the reason it’s evolved to where it is today can be clearly seen in this match.

00:14:30.830 --> 00:14:38.390
It’s not just the attacks, it's the amazing strength one finds in the very human instinct of self-defense.

00:14:38.390 --> 00:14:41.400
And right now, this young man has shown with his body

00:14:41.400 --> 00:14:46.670
that this sport truly is “King of all Sports,” beyond a shadow of a doubt.

00:15:35.910 --> 00:15:37.920
Joe, are you all right?

00:15:44.280 --> 00:15:45.300
Don’t mind me.

00:15:45.300 --> 00:15:47.290
Go tend to Ao, old man.

00:15:55.420 --> 00:15:57.170
Aoyama-kun!

00:16:42.760 --> 00:16:50.640
Joe... the fact that you won means that there’s once again a chance that you’ll fight the great Rikiishi.

00:16:50.640 --> 00:16:52.960
But, on the other hand, Danpei-san…

00:16:52.960 --> 00:16:57.150
It looks like your little plan has produced results far beyond your wildest dreams.

00:17:23.130 --> 00:17:25.230
So, old man, why’d you call me out here?

00:17:25.230 --> 00:17:27.940
U-Um, what would you wish to discuss with us?

00:17:30.100 --> 00:17:32.350
Shit, what’s up? Moping around like that…

00:17:32.350 --> 00:17:33.670
I’ve come this far to see you.

00:17:33.670 --> 00:17:35.560
Look at these scars. These bandages.

00:17:35.560 --> 00:17:37.120
I really should be in intensive care.

00:17:43.470 --> 00:17:46.120
Aoyama-kun… and Joe.

00:17:48.120 --> 00:17:49.540
I really am…

00:17:49.540 --> 00:17:52.130
I really am sorry for how I've treated you both!

00:17:52.130 --> 00:17:53.670
O-Old man?

00:17:53.670 --> 00:17:55.180
D-Danpei-sensei?

00:17:55.180 --> 00:17:58.020
Please… find it in your hearts to forgive this old oaf.

00:18:00.820 --> 00:18:02.410
Hey, wait a minute, old man.

00:18:03.130 --> 00:18:05.190
Why’re ya apologizing?

00:18:03.540 --> 00:18:05.190
<i>What are you suggesting you did wrong, Sir?</i>

00:18:06.280 --> 00:18:10.050
Until today, I’ve been fighting an internal battle.

00:18:10.050 --> 00:18:13.030
I wondered just how far I should go playing with other people’s hearts and dreams.

00:18:13.030 --> 00:18:15.190
Even though it was all for Joe’s sake…

00:18:15.190 --> 00:18:16.790
For my sake?

00:18:18.160 --> 00:18:19.330
That’s right.

00:18:19.330 --> 00:18:20.930
It was for your sake, Joe.

00:18:20.930 --> 00:18:24.160
I was only using Aoyama-kun to make you stronger!

00:18:33.650 --> 00:18:35.670
What the hell are ya trying to say, old man?

00:18:38.090 --> 00:18:39.250
It was for boxing!

00:18:39.250 --> 00:18:41.440
Everything was for the sake of boxing!

00:18:41.440 --> 00:18:43.180
Boxing is <i>everything</i> to me!

00:18:45.410 --> 00:18:48.880
The reason I treated you badly, and shoved you away from me…

00:18:48.880 --> 00:18:52.050
was because I had a duty to boxing to treat you that way so you would become better.

00:18:52.050 --> 00:18:54.280
A duty as your coach...

00:18:59.740 --> 00:19:03.040
Listen, Joe, in the martial arts world, we have this saying:

00:19:03.770 --> 00:19:06.590
“Even the most ordinary coach equals ten fighters.”

00:19:06.590 --> 00:19:08.900
Which means, a boxer can be as aggressive as he wants,

00:19:08.900 --> 00:19:11.680
but without the technical backing of a coach, he’ll just be an aggressor.

00:19:11.680 --> 00:19:14.570
He’ll never learn how to defend himself.

00:19:14.570 --> 00:19:17.050
After all, those who take up fighting in the first place

00:19:17.050 --> 00:19:19.960
tend to be stronger and more aggressive than normal people.

00:19:19.960 --> 00:19:24.140
They can learn how to punch and kick on their own.

00:19:24.140 --> 00:19:26.580
But they never learn to defend themselves.

00:19:26.580 --> 00:19:28.450
Or rather, they never attempt to learn.

00:19:28.450 --> 00:19:32.420
Even if they <i>do</i> learn, when it's time to fight, the fire overcomes them and everything slips away.

00:19:32.420 --> 00:19:34.890
And someone who’s very guilty of that is <i>you</i>, Joe.

00:19:37.360 --> 00:19:41.350
As a coach, as just an ordinary guy, I found myself in front of a big wall.

00:19:43.960 --> 00:19:45.370
It was then, that…

00:19:47.130 --> 00:19:48.370
Y-You mean me?

00:19:49.250 --> 00:19:51.370
I used you.

00:19:51.370 --> 00:19:53.820
B-Because I’m weak,

00:19:53.820 --> 00:19:55.880
and it would be easier to teach me defense moves?

00:19:55.880 --> 00:19:58.650
Yes, you are weak.

00:19:58.650 --> 00:20:01.820
But you are blessed with a passion to become strong.

00:20:01.820 --> 00:20:04.860
You have the perfect temperament to be trained for defense.

00:20:04.860 --> 00:20:07.580
It was my plan to teach you the perfect defensive technique

00:20:07.580 --> 00:20:10.740
so that Joe would be mocked by it, and would then be forced to discover how to defend himself.

00:20:10.740 --> 00:20:12.910
It’s the easiest way to beat that technique into him.

00:20:12.910 --> 00:20:14.990
It was all just an act to help Joe discover it on his own.

00:20:15.860 --> 00:20:19.330
But my plan gave birth to something far bigger than I could have anticipated.

00:20:19.330 --> 00:20:22.870
To protect his own body, without instruction from anyone, and with little regard to how he looked,

00:20:22.870 --> 00:20:25.970
Joe used a defensive stance and tricky footwork.

00:20:26.600 --> 00:20:30.950
I don’t think you could have done better, even if you had been taught by the best coach.

00:20:32.700 --> 00:20:37.240
And I wanted Joe to fall into a pit where he was all alone and no one tried to help him

00:20:37.240 --> 00:20:40.280
so he could learn to climb out of that cruel hell all by himself.

00:20:41.020 --> 00:20:44.140
The fight against loneliness, the countless defensive techniques, they were all…

00:20:45.660 --> 00:20:47.830
They were all For the Sake of Tomorrow lessons.

00:20:47.830 --> 00:20:49.890
It was the sixth… and the seventh!

00:20:51.170 --> 00:20:53.180
Joe, you did well.

00:20:53.180 --> 00:20:55.250
I’m so proud of you for standing up to it!

00:20:55.250 --> 00:20:56.550
You did well…

00:20:56.550 --> 00:20:57.540
You did well.

00:21:18.220 --> 00:21:19.290
Aoyama-kun.

00:21:20.150 --> 00:21:21.170
Yes, Sir?

00:21:23.940 --> 00:21:25.320
To you…

00:21:25.320 --> 00:21:27.460
I must be… I must be…

00:21:27.460 --> 00:21:29.420
No. Don’t even say it.

00:21:29.420 --> 00:21:34.620
You took me in, even though I’m such a weakling, and told me I could be successful if I tried!

00:21:34.620 --> 00:21:35.720
Aoyama-kun!

00:21:36.520 --> 00:21:40.480
Th-That’s become a valuable lesson that I will carry with me for the rest of my life!

00:21:40.970 --> 00:21:42.490
Aoyama-kun!

00:21:43.990 --> 00:21:47.020
Thank you for putting up with me for so long.

00:22:14.660 --> 00:22:16.980
Joe, what’s gotten into you!?

00:22:26.940 --> 00:22:27.980
Hey, Ao.

00:22:29.370 --> 00:22:30.450
Joe!

00:22:30.450 --> 00:22:31.930
Joe, what was that…

00:22:31.930 --> 00:22:33.450
Leave me alone for a while.

00:22:36.450 --> 00:22:37.680
Listen, Ao,

00:22:37.680 --> 00:22:39.950
I know I’ve hated you and made fun of you.

00:22:39.950 --> 00:22:41.930
But, I’m sorry. I was wrong.

00:22:41.930 --> 00:22:43.010
Yabuki-san!

00:22:43.010 --> 00:22:46.010
When we fought, your punches really got to me.

00:22:46.010 --> 00:22:48.370
I thought I’d have to give up countless times.

00:22:48.370 --> 00:22:49.470
I’ll never make fun of you again.

00:22:49.470 --> 00:22:51.190
I won’t let other people make fun of you either.

00:22:51.190 --> 00:22:54.470
Though I guess only an idiot would make fun of you now.

00:22:54.850 --> 00:22:56.210
And as for you, old man...

00:22:57.930 --> 00:22:58.980
I guess I've learned…

00:23:00.090 --> 00:23:02.440
that I’m a real blockhead. Really.

00:23:03.960 --> 00:23:05.850
But I’m tired of just farting around.

00:23:07.550 --> 00:23:08.750
I wanna become stronger.

00:23:08.750 --> 00:23:11.150
And I want you to help me do that.

00:23:12.380 --> 00:23:14.450
I won’t lose to Rikiishi, either.

00:23:15.400 --> 00:23:16.950
Joe!

00:24:35.850 --> 00:24:37.530
The day of Rikiishi’s release from the Juvenile Prison is set.

00:24:38.010 --> 00:24:42.540
Rikiishi and Joe climb into a rain-soaked ring to settle their earlier draw.

00:24:43.300 --> 00:24:45.910
Yohko writes it off as a small, insignificant match.

00:24:45.910 --> 00:24:46.540
However!

00:24:47.140 --> 00:24:50.580
